# Track J regression net — Guard[Vector[String]].get() axis-cell (heap UAF,
# NOT double-free): the shallow header copy aliased the guard's array, then
# scope-exit `gorget_array_free` on the loaded local walked the (already
# element-freed) backing again → `gorget_string_free invariant: cap=<garbage>
# but alloc=NULL` (exit 1). Post-fix: View tag → no shadow drop.
#
# HEAP-FORCED elements (`"a-forced"` etc. via `push`) — each String slot has a
# real heap `alloc`, so the invalid re-walk actually poisons memory.
Vector[String] make():
    Vector[String] v = []
    v.push("a-forced")
    v.push("b-forced")
    return v

void main():
    Mutex[Vector[String]] m = Mutex[Vector[String]](make())
    Guard[Vector[String]] g = m.lock()
    print(g.get().len())
